    ^{:line 106 :doc "Importer is present for backward-compatibility. Calling\nImport(path) is the same as calling ImportFrom(path, \"\", 0);\ni.e., locally vendored packages may not be found.\nThe types package does not call Import if an ImporterFrom\nis present.\n"} Importer










    (^{:doc "ImportFrom returns the imported package for the given import\npath when imported by a package file located in dir.\nIf the import failed, besides returning an error, ImportFrom\nis encouraged to cache and return a package anyway, if one\nwas created. This will reduce package inconsistencies and\nfollow-on type checker errors due to the missing package.\nThe mode value must be 0; it is reserved for future use.\nTwo calls to ImportFrom with the same path and dir must\nreturn the same package.\n"} ImportFrom [^string path ^string dir ^ImportMode mode] :results [(* Package) error])))




