    ^{:line 256 :tag (map (* ast/Ident) Object) :doc "Defs maps identifiers to the objects they define (including\npackage names, dots \".\" of dot-imports, and blank \"_\" identifiers).\nFor identifiers that do not denote objects (e.g., the package name\nin package clauses, or symbolic variables t in t := x.(type) of\ntype switch headers), the corresponding objects are nil.\n\nFor an embedded field, Defs returns the field *Var it defines.\n\nIn ill-typed code, such as a duplicate declaration of the\nsame name, Defs may lack an entry for a declaring identifier.\n\nInvariant: Defs[id] == nil || Defs[id].Pos() == id.Pos()\n"} Defs






    ^{:line 263 :tag (map (* ast/Ident) Object) :doc "Uses maps identifiers to the objects they denote.\n\nFor an embedded field, Uses returns the *TypeName it denotes.\n\nInvariant: Uses[id].Pos() != id.Pos()\n"} Uses










    ^{:line 274 :tag (map ast/Node Object) :doc "Implicits maps nodes to their implicitly declared objects, if any.\nThe following node and object types may appear:\n\n    node               declared object\n\n    *ast.ImportSpec    *PkgName for imports without renames\n    *ast.CaseClause    type-specific *Var for each type switch case clause (incl. default)\n    *ast.Field         anonymous parameter *Var (incl. unnamed results)\n"} Implicits



    ^{:line 278 :tag (map (* ast/SelectorExpr) (* Selection)) :doc "Selections maps selector expressions (excluding qualified identifiers)\nto their corresponding selections.\n"} Selections


































    ^{:line 313 :tag (map ast/Node (* Scope)) :doc "Scopes maps ast.Nodes to the scopes they define. Package scopes are not\nassociated with a specific node but with all files belonging to a package.\nThus, the package scope can be found in the type-checked Package object.\nScopes nest, with the Universe scope being the outermost scope, enclosing\nthe package scope, which contains (one or more) files scopes, which enclose\nfunction scopes which in turn enclose statement and function literal scopes.\nNote that even though package-level functions are declared in the package\nscope, the function scopes are embedded in the file scope of the file\ncontaining the function declaration.\n\nThe Scope of a function contains the declarations of any\ntype parameters, parameters, and named results, plus any\nlocal declarations in the body block.\nIt is coextensive with the complete extent of the\nfunction's syntax ([*ast.FuncDecl] or [*ast.FuncLit]).\nThe Scopes mapping does not contain an entry for the\nfunction body ([*ast.BlockStmt]); the function's scope is\nassociated with the [*ast.FuncType].\n\nThe following node types may appear in Scopes:\n\n    *ast.File\n    *ast.FuncType\n    *ast.TypeSpec\n    *ast.BlockStmt\n    *ast.IfStmt\n    *ast.SwitchStmt\n    *ast.TypeSwitchStmt\n    *ast.CaseClause\n    *ast.CommClause\n    *ast.ForStmt\n    *ast.RangeStmt\n"} Scopes






    ^{:line 320 :tag (slice (* Initializer)) :doc "InitOrder is the list of package-level initializers in the order in which\nthey must be executed. Initializers referring to variables related by an\ninitialization dependency appear in topological order, the others appear\nin source order. Variables without an initialization expression do not\nappear in this list.\n"} InitOrder






